# No types are written; the calls in sight give the key two written texts, and the front end widens what it has seen to `string`. So something was expected of the key, and it held no name: the read under the key stayed one
# generic operation, the turns ran other code and the loop was built once. "Any text" says nothing of names: the names of the holder's one layout are asked there as where nothing is expected; each is tested at the run.
# RUN(WIRE): print
# WIRE: function f1 name="total" {{*}} {type=undefined|null|string flags=[IsExpected]}
# RUN(HEADS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# HEADS-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# HEADS-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# The event is counted once in each copy of the loop: in the typed copy the names are compared in front of it, and the other copy, which opens its guesses, asks them by one switch in the turn.
# RUN(EVENT): compile AccessesDispatchedByKeyString mechanisms=all
# EVENT: statistic AccessesDispatchedByKeyString 2
# RUN(BOTH): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# BOTH: SwitchString {{*}} strings=
# BOTH-COUNT-3: = ValueEqualsLiteral
